# Alias usage (admin-dashboard)

## General

- Use **`@/`** for anything under `src/` that does not have a dedicated short alias below (configured in `vite.config.js` and `jsconfig.json`).
- Prefer these aliases over long relative paths (`../../../`).

## Short aliases (shared / reusable UI)

| Alias | Resolves to | Typical imports |
|-------|-------------|-----------------|
| `@datagrid` | `src/components/datagrid` | `import { DataGrid } from '@datagrid'` |
| `@common` | `src/components/common` | `import { SectionHeader } from '@common'`, `import X from '@common/ErrorBoundary'` |
| `@charts` | `src/components/charts` | `import { SimpleBarChart } from '@charts'` |
| `@branding` | `src/components/branding` | `import DukaLogo from '@branding/DukaLogo'` |
| `@widgets` | `src/components/mui` | `import NotificationProvider from '@widgets/feedback/NotificationProvider'` |

## Rules

- **Do not** add an alias named `@mui` — it would clash with **`@mui/material`** and **`@mui/icons-material`** from `node_modules`.
- When adding a new top-level reusable folder under `components/`, add matching entries in **both** `vite.config.js` (`resolve.alias`) and `jsconfig.json` (`compilerOptions.paths`), then extend this table.
- AG Grid–specific renderers, editors, and filters live under `@datagrid`; re-export from `@datagrid/index.js` when they should be imported from the package root.
- **Feature grids** (columns + grid logic for one screen) live under `src/components/<feature>/Grid/` with `columnConfig.js` and `index.jsx`; import the folder via `@/components/<feature>/Grid` (see `grid-implementation.mdc`).
